stname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96cbfc8a-5747-527b-870e-cde711211b9b', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96cbfc8a-5747-527b-870e-cde711211b9b'}, {'abstract': 'Zurich’s fourth district, a former red-light area next to the main railway station, brims with shops and cafes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/travel/five-places-to-go-in-zurich-switzerland-kreis-district.html', 'snippet': 'Zurich’s fourth district, a former red-light area next to the main railway station, brims with shops and cafes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sleazy bars. Sex shops. Streetwalkers. That was long the dodgy mix in Zurich’s fourth district, known locally as Kreis 4, a sprawling red-light area next to the city’s main railway station. Switzerland’s largest city, however, is gambling on an ambitious development known as Europaallee to burnish the neighborhood’s style and reputation. In addition to housing and office space, this new district, scheduled for completion in 2021, is already brimming with clothing boutiques, concept stores, cafes and restaurants, many devoted to native Swiss designers and delicacies. As Europaallee rises, Kreis 4 is increasingly on the right side of the tracks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/29/travel/29SURFACING1/29SURFACING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/01/29/travel/29SURFACING1/29SURFACING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/29/travel/29SURFACING1/29SURFACING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {