ed about Barney the dinosaur.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/arts/dance/andrea-kleines-new-work-focuses-on-torture-and-music.html', 'snippet': 'The work, “My Dinner With Andrea,” confirms what some have always suspected about Barney the dinosaur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do the Bee Gees, Metallica, Christina Aguilera and Barney the purple dinosaur have in common? Apparently, their songs have all been used as tools of torture by the United States military. In Andrea Kleine’s new work, “My Dinner With Andrea: The Piece Formerly Known as Torture Playlist,” pop songs mix with an original score by Bobby Previte as she and six other performers explore the overlap of choreographic and torture techniques — repetition, obsession, release — and confront society’s complicity.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE3/05GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andrea Kleine’s New Work Focuses on Torture and Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Of Torture and the Bee Gees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kleine, Andrea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Dinner With Andrea: The Piece Formerly Known as Torture Playlist (Dance)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-01T20:24:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e47ad042-3ff3-5586-acff-e562e28c707a', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e47ad042-3ff3-5586-acff-e562e28c707a'}, {'abstract': 'A two-part exhibition, “Common Time,” is opening at the Walker Art Center in Minneapolis and the Museum of Contemporary Art in Chicago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/arts/design/merce-cunningham-looking-beyond-the-movement.html', 'snippet': 'A two-part exhibition, “Common Time,” is opening at the Walker Art Center in Minneapolis and the Museum of Contemporary Art in Chicago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Merce Cunningham died in 2009, he decided his dance company would die with him. So, in 2011, after a final tour, it did. Yet a wealth of his art remains in circulation. Other companies perform his dances, and this week two American museums will open surveys devoted to his dance-related work.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 592}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2020, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE7/05GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Merce Cunningham, Looking Beyond the Movement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art; Looking Beyond the Movement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walker Art Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-01T20:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56a0f151-899a-5713-9591-91a13a71d8b7', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56a0f151-899a-5713-9591-91a13a71d8b7'}, {'abstract': 'Several police officers were hurt Thursday as they evacuated Amona, and Israel’s prime minister vowed to build a new settlement elsewhere in the West Bank.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/world/middleeast/amona-west-bank-settlers-eviction.html', 'snippet': 'Several police officers were hurt Thursday as they evacuated Amona, and Israel’s prime minister vowed to build a new settlement elsewhere in the West Bank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of angry protesters confronted Israeli police officers as they tried to eject them Thursday from the illegal West Bank settlement of Amona, the second day of clashes there. Several officers were injured as they cleared a synagogue of 200 people who had barricaded themselves in the outpost’s last inhabited building.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/world/europe/03amona-slide-JFBI/03amona-slide-JFBI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Ejects Settlers in Last Stand at West Bank Synagogue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-photo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-01T20:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea89ea7a-43bf-5305-8fe4-ca38e95468bb', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea89ea7a-43bf-5305-8fe4-ca38e95468bb'}, {'abstract': 'The FXX series started Season 12 on an attention-getting note by turning the cast black, and now comes a scalding dispute over a gay slur.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/arts/television/its-always-sunny-just-keeps-getting-bolder.html', 'snippet': 'The FXX series started Season 12 on an attention-getting note by turning the cast black, and now comes a scalding dispute over a gay slur.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s Always Sunny in Philadelphia” is in the midst of yet another outrageous season, its 12th, and on Wednesday night, Feb. 8, things get particularly ear-burning in an episode called “Hero or Hate Crime?” The series, on FXX, is about five friends who operate a bar in Philadelphia. The season premiere in January was pretty over the top — the five, who are white, were turned black by an electrical shock as they were watching “The Wiz,” and a semi-musical exploration of racial stereotyping ensued. The Feb. 8 installment is at least as boundary-pushing. It begins with a falling piano, a shouted gay slur and a windblown scratch-off lottery ticket. The five take their dispute over ownership of the ticket to professional arbiters, and the resulting debate about what does and does not constitute a slur would curl George Carlin’s toes. The episode also gives the props department a chance to make indescribably vulgar alterations to an exercise bicycle, and by its end one of the core five, Mac (Rob McElhenney), may have had a personal breakthrough 12 seasons in the making.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1999, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE5/05GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘It’s Always Sunny’ Just Keeps Getting Bolder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; Putting Slurs to the Test', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FXX (TV Network)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia (TV Program)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-01T20:32:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06632af1-3bde-5a58-b971-ec9790c98128', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06632af1-3bde-5a58-b971-ec9790c98128'}, {'abstract': 'Underthings that suit you. And just in time for Valentine’s Day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2017/02/01/fashion/new-lingerie-intimates-shopping.html', 'snippet': 'Underthings that suit you. And just in time for Valentine’s Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Underthings that suit you. And just in time for Valentine’s Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/fashion/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 230, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/02/fashion/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 230}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/fashion/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/fashion/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT/02BROWSE-PICTURE-IMPERFECT-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legac