/02/01/us/texas-transgender-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Jess Herbst posted a message on the town website of New Hope, Tex., saying that she had transitioned and would no longer be known as Jeff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just days before a public town meeting on Tuesday night, Jess Herbst, the mayor of New Hope, Tex., had an official announcement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/02/us/02-transgendermayor/02xp-transgendermayor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1538, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Mayor Announces That She Is Transgender', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Message From City Hall in Texas: ‘Yes I Am Transgender and a Seated Mayor’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-01T20:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b04abbd-90e4-5f67-b60c-1703ef029712', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b04abbd-90e4-5f67-b60c-1703ef029712'}, {'abstract': 'On Feb. 10, the stars align at all three of Carnegie Hall’s spaces, at the Metropolitan Opera, and in Philadelphia, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/arts/music/a-full-carnegie-hall-and-more-in-the-northeast.html', 'snippet': 'On Feb. 10, the stars align at all three of Carnegie Hall’s spaces, at the Metropolitan Opera, and in Philadelphia, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some nights it just happens: The musical world aligns to give listeners a burst of exciting offerings. Friday, Feb. 10, presents some tough choices for classical fans in the Northeast corridor. All three of Carnegie Hall’s performance spaces are filled. The extraordinary pianist Igor Levit makes his Carnegie debut in Zankel Hall with Beethoven’s “Diabelli” Variations, three prelude-fugue pairings by Shostakovich and a new work by Frederic Rzewski. Upstairs in the intimate Weill Hall, the charming soprano Anna Lucia Richter gives a recital of songs by Schumann, Brahms and Britten. And in the biggest room, Stern Auditorium, the American Symphony Orchestra under Leon Botstein delves into lesser-known 20th-century Czech works. (carnegiehall.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1179, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE1/05GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Full Carnegie Hall and More in the Northeast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical; The Stars Align in the Northeast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'sub