02/01/movies/albert-brookss-modern-romance-and-other-valentines-day-massacres.html', 'snippet': 'This annual bill at Anthology Film Archives features two Elaine May movies and an insecure man fretting about love.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Modern Romance,” Albert Brooks’s 1981 comedy, isn’t so modern anymore (so many phone booths!), but the humor is still startlingly deadpan, and its portrait of uncertainty about love and commitment still resonates. The film, starring and directed by Mr. Brooks, has a three-screening revisiting beginning Friday, Feb. 10, at Anthology Film Archives in the East Village as part of the annual “Valentine’s Day Massacre,” a quirky selection of movies loosely about love. It’s paired with Maurice Pialat’s “We Won’t Grow Old Together,” another film featuring an unstable couple. The lineup also includes two Elaine May films, “The Heartbreak Kid” and “A New Leaf,” as well as Andrzej Zulawski’s “Possession.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 240}