d2d76-e1e9-5e12-a943-3feaca57ba78', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28fd2d76-e1e9-5e12-a943-3feaca57ba78'}, {'abstract': 'The Mac operating system often tucks an unused scroll bar out of sight, but that can be changed in the settings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/02/technology/personaltech/solving-the-case-of-the-disappearing-scroll-bars.html', 'snippet': 'The Mac operating system often tucks an unused scroll bar out of sight, but that can be changed in the settings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I recently switched to a Mac laptop, and the Safari browser confuses me. Sometimes it has scroll bars on the side of the page, and sometimes it doesn’t. Why is this?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Solving the Case of the Mac’s Disappearing Scroll Bars', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web Browsers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mac OS (Operating System)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iOS (Operating System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-02T17:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4c186cb-d89b-56f5-b8c1-df4089037a8b', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4c186cb-d89b-56f5-b8c1-df4089037a8b'}, {'abstract': 'A contentious phone call with the Australian prime minister set off a political storm there at a time many residents say they want closer ties to China.', 'web_url': 'https://ww