2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-02T22:17:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/724957a3-f484-5ae1-b82a-06e801c15d89', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/724957a3-f484-5ae1-b82a-06e801c15d89'}, {'abstract': 'Our chief dance critic looks at this troupe’s changing lineups, including young dancers making their debuts in leading roles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/02/arts/dance/debuts-new-faces-and-bodies-in-classic-roles-at-new-york-city-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'Our chief dance critic looks at this troupe’s changing lineups, including young dancers making their debuts in leading roles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No performing art is more dependent on — more differentiated by — the individual contributions of its interpreters than ballet. If you don’t feel this art’s spell, try seeing any important classical work with two or more different casts in a top-level company. At New York City Ballet (more than with any other troupe), a constant element is the promotion of young talent to leading roles. Not so infrequently, you can see a junior dancer from the corps de ballet and a senior ballerina tackle the same star role on consecutive days.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/arts/03PRODIGALDEBUT/03PRODIGALDEBUT-thumbStandar