abstract': 'Streams like the one from the Kilauea volcano usually last a day or two, but this one has flowed since New Year’s Eve. And visitors have to keep their distance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/02/science/hawaii-lava-stream.html', 'snippet': 'Streams like the one from the Kilauea volcano usually last a day or two, but this one has flowed since New Year’s Eve. And visitors have to keep their distance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Off the coast of the island of Hawaii, hundreds of millions of gallons of lava are flowing into the ocean like blood from a ruptured artery. Starting in January at Kīlauea Volcano’s Kamokuna ocean entry, the lava hit the salty water, shooting molten rock upward and outward, accompanied by a rising, steamy cloud of acid.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Streaming Lava, Collapsing Cliffs and a Hawaii Volcano’s Spectacular Show', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'River of Fire: Where Lava Met Cool Blue Ocean', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Ocean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-03T00:13:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ae3bdb3-69f7-5f77-9f07-a6b05c2f1536', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ae3bdb3-69f7-5f77-9f07-a6b05c2f1536'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rosen’s legacy as an electrical engineer and inventor is the roughly 600 geostationary satellites that handle TV signals and other data.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/02/business/harold-rosen-dead-engineer-satellite.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rosen’s legacy as an electrical engineer and inventor is the roughly 600 geostationary satellites that handle TV signals and other data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you are reading these words online or in print, there is a strong chance that Harold A. Rosen played a part in getting them to you. Mr. Rosen, who died on Monday at 90 at his home in Pacific Palisades, Calif., was a driving force in the invention of modern communication satellite technology.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/03rosen-obit/03rosen-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/03/business/03rosen-obit/03rosen-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/03rosen-obit/03rosen-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/03rosen-obit/03rosen-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/03/business/03rosen-obit/03rosen-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 764}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/03rosen-obit/03rosen-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':