se boundaries might be as simple as walking on a hand rail. Make sure it’s sturdy and stable. Wear shoes with thin soles or go barefoot. “That gives you a more tactile feel and allows your feet to interact with the rail,” Graves says. Being on a rail is similar to being on a balance beam, but because the former is thinner and usually round, your whole foot cannot be on top of the rail at once. “That makes balance one of the biggest challenges,” Graves says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05mag-05tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1043, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05mag-05tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1043}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05mag-05tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 590, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05mag-05tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05tip/05tip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Walk on Hand Rails', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Walk on Hand Rails', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parkour (Sport)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-03T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jaime Lowe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaime', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00287e1a-a75b-5be0-8c9f-641a12723f1f', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00287e1a-a75b-5be0-8c9f-641a12723f1f'}, {'abstract': 'A piece of tofurkey between two slices of frozen bread does not a proper meal make.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/03/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-rules-on-a-sad-desk-lunch.html', 'snippet': 'A piece of tofurkey between two slices of frozen bread does not a proper meal make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel writes: For the last five years, my romantic partner, Stephanie, has been making the same terrible lunch to bring to work. She has a longstanding habit of unceremoniously dropping a few slices of Tofurky between 2 pieces of frozen bread, using no condiments. She eats this depression sandwich alone in her cubicle. In the past she has expressed envy over the sandwiches I prepare for myself. I would like you to compel Stephanie to devote the energy required to make a better sandwich.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/magazine/05hodgman/05hodgman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail'