': 'nyt://article/6c06a3a7-0bb5-562e-987c-3f23b3451a5e', 'word_count': 2505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c06a3a7-0bb5-562e-987c-3f23b3451a5e'}, {'abstract': 'Still, no matter which side you favored in the latest executive-order controversy, wasn’t it good to see companies back on their heels a bit?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/03/your-money/uber-and-starbucks-protests-show-boycotts-need-more-than-a-hashtag.html', 'snippet': 'Still, no matter which side you favored in the latest executive-order controversy, wasn’t it good to see companies back on their heels a bit?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the race to find someone — anyone — to lash out at over the immigration and travel restrictions ordered by President Trump last Friday, many consumers settled on an odd target: Uber. It had, supposedly, undercut prices for non-Uber taxis just as protesting taxi drivers went back to work. A boycott brigade formed almost immediately.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/04MONEY1/04MONEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/03/business/04MONEY1/04MONEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/04MONEY1/04MONEY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/03/business/04MONEY1/04MONEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/03/business/04MONEY1/04MONEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600,