investors’ hopes of quick economic growth, at least for now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Donald J. Trump won the presidential election, investors seemed positively giddy about what he was going to do to improve the nation’s economy. Believing that his promises to reduce corporate taxes and curtail costly regulations would unleash economic growth, investors pushed stock indexes to new heights.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/04/business/05GRET/05GRET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1268, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trump Effect: What’s an Investor to Do?', 'kicker': 'Fair Game', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trump Effect: Time to Buckle Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-03T18:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f58e6b-7864-5862-91b0-5e276425356d', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f58e6b-7864-5862-91b0-5e276425356d'}, {'abstract': 'A Kelly Wearstler lamp in marble and brass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/03/t-magazine/design/kelly-wearstler-task-lamp.html', 'snippet': 'A Kelly Wearstler lamp in marble and brass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Edison is celebrated for his invention of the practical light bulb, but in truth, this came roughly a year after a British chemist named Joseph Swan debuted a similar bulb in 1878. Edison’s innovation was longer lasting, evolving to illuminate the modern world, but Swan’s elegant lamp prototype, which burned for only about 40 hours, was a shapely marvel. Today, the designer Kelly Wearstler has created a minimalist task lamp in antique burnished brass that echoes his ephemeral creation. A can-shaped shade on an adjustable arm hovers above a base of cylindr