for its many layers of editing, but fundamental change appears likely to come soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE NEW YORK TIMES has a reputation for impeccable editing. Not just because it can turn one particular story into a showpiece, but because it achieves a high level of consistency and polish across its entire report. It’s part of what readers pay for, and what they’ve come to expect.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1453, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/sunday-review/05pubed/05pubed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hard Look at Times Editing in the Digital Era', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Readying The Times for Editing 3.0', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-04T19:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/acd84204-a582-595f-8968-a71f09c00431', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acd84204-a582-595f-8968-a71f09c00431'}, {'abstract': 'The growth of legalized gambling is triggering a comparable boom in devastated lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/04/opinion/threatened-with-ruin-at-the-virtual-casino.html', 'snippet': 'The growth of legalized gambling is triggering a comparable boom in devastated lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was fantastic at such an early hour of the morning to be hailed by a beautiful woman in a low-cut red gown asking, “Feeling lucky?” But of course the woman leaning over the blackjack table was just another electronic fantasy at the video-steeped Resorts World gambling casino on the outer fringes of Queens.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/05/opinion/05sun3web/05sun3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/05/opinion/05sun3web/05sun