alue': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-06T00:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ccf0b1-d4f5-5a77-b019-d2e7f2d73b89', 'word_count': 1461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ccf0b1-d4f5-5a77-b019-d2e7f2d73b89'}, {'abstract': 'The president says he wants to favor the victims of religious persecution, but his order would cut the number of such refugees the country admits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/05/opinion/donald-trumps-phony-compassion-for-christians.html', 'snippet': 'The president says he wants to favor the victims of religious persecution, but his order would cut the number of such refugees the country admits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the summer of 2014, the Islamic State seized a region of northern Iraq where people of different religions and ethnic groups had coexisted since biblical times, and sought to cleanse it of everyone who was not a Sunni Muslim. ISIS killed or enslaved thousands of Yazidis and massacred Shiite Muslims. The group readily admitted that it wanted to eradicate Christianity from the Middle East. In a matter of days, more than 100,000 Iraqi Christians had fled their homes, mostly to Iraqi Kurdistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/06/opinion/06malinowski-inyt/06malinowski-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im