anizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Erbil (Iraq)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinjar (Iraq)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-06T00:37:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Malinowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malinowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bf0bcbe-67fa-5e83-af55-7c7cfc7bf553', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bf0bcbe-67fa-5e83-af55-7c7cfc7bf553'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s adversaries in the U.S. are not confused, fragmented, demoralized or alone. That’s an advantage in their battle against Trumpism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/05/opinion/five-reasons-the-opposition-is-in-good-shape-to-fight-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s adversaries in the U.S. are not confused, fragmented, demoralized or alone. That’s an advantage in their battle against Trumpism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMHERST, Mass. — President Trump’s first weeks in office left a majority of Americans appalled. With his “alternative facts,” his scapegoating of foreigners and international trade, and his barrage of executive orders, Mr. Trump confirmed what the opposition had feared: that he will run the country like a populist autocrat and paranoid protectionist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/06/opinion/06corrales2-inyt/06corrales2-inyt-thumbStandar