icle', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kin Woo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24713bc8-9794-5055-bdfc-8ac6bf7f0e27', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24713bc8-9794-5055-bdfc-8ac6bf7f0e27'}, {'abstract': 'The city of Al Bab, occupied by the Islamic State, is being squeezed from all sides by Turkish-backed rebels and Russian-backed government forces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/06/world/middleeast/syria-isis-al-bab.html', 'snippet': 'The city of Al Bab, occupied by the Islamic State, is being squeezed from all sides by Turkish-backed rebels and Russian-backed government forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An important northern Syrian city held by the Islamic State, the group’s last major outpost in the region, was practically surrounded Monday by pro-government and insurgent forces squeezing it from different directions, according to rebels and the state-run Syrian news media.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/07/world/07syria1/07syria1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/07/world/07syria1/07syria1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/07/world/07syria1/07syria1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/