 Rauschenberg’s set pieces strapped to the roof of their Volkswagen Microbus — to perform “Antic Meet” at the Walker Art Center. This month, the museum unveils a major retrospective, “Merce Cunningham: Common Time,” co-presented with the Museum of Contemporary Art Chicago. The pioneering choreographer was known for collaborating with artists (Jasper Johns, Bruce Nauman), which helped dance enter major museums, many of which are now outfitting new spaces with black boxes and sprung floors for just such performances. “Ephemeral forms have largely been left out of art history,” the show’s co-curator Philip Bither says. “And it’s important that those stories be told.” In addition to sets and costumes, the exhibit will feature performances and new commissions from such contemporary choreographers as Rashaun Mitchell and Silas Riener, who met as dancers in the Merce Cunningham Dance Company, as well as Maria Hassabi and Beth Gill. Happily, the Merce moment will extend eastward in April, with the French company CNDC-Angers set to perform a full evening of Cunningham works at the Joyce Theater in New York, and the Paris Opera Ballet staging his Duchamp-inspired classic “Walkaround Time.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '108', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 543}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 927, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/t-magazine/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0/19tmag-01look_merce-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1855, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Original Artists’ Choreographer, Back in the Spotlight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaps and Bounds ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-07T15:26:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Merrell Hambleton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Merrell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hambleton', 'q