education-secretary-confirmed.html', 'snippet': 'The vote on Tuesday was believed to be the first in Senate history in which the vice president was called in to break a tie on a cabinet nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Betsy DeVos, a wealthy Republican donor with almost no experience in public education, was confirmed by the Senate as the nation’s education secretary on Tuesday, but only with the help of a historic tiebreaking vote from Vice President Mike Pence after weeks of protests and two defections within her own party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Betsy DeVos Confirmed as Education Secretary; Pence Breaks Tie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DeVos Confirmed for Education by Pence’s Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeVos, Elizabeth (1958- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-07T17:29:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman and Yamiche Alcindor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Yamiche', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alcindor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85c29612-8a8a-5ff8-ad17-bb3586c511b9', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85c29612-8a8a-5ff8-ad17-bb3586c511b9'}, {'abstract': 'Spoilers lie ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/07/watching/jane-the-virgin-michael-twist-chapter-54.html', 'snippet': 'Spoilers lie ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just months after defying its title with an episode in which Jane loses her virginity, The CW’s high-concept telenovela, “Jane the Virgin,” once again has fans flipping out all over social media. The Feb. 6 episode, “Chapter Fifty-Four,” delivered what may be the show’s biggest shock to date. For those who have already watched it and need some help processing, here’s a spoiler-filled roundup of essential responses and interviews, plus an open letter from the showrunner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/07/watching/07jane/07jane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/07/watching/07jane/07jane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/07/watching/07jane/07jane-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/07/watching/07jane/07jane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/07/watching/07jane/07jane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/07/watching/07jane/07jane-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType'