ppet': 'Also, a new spot from Roberto Deiaco of Armani Ristorante, chefs on the move and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAILY PROVISIONS Coffee and food to eat in or take out are sold next to Union Square Cafe from what may be about the smallest restaurant David Rockwell ever designed — some people have more spacious kitchens in their apartments. But Daily Provisions is extremely well tailored, done in marine blue wainscoting with marble counters and tables, a few seats and shelves full of freshly baked breads, glazed and sugared crullers, cookies and croissants flecked with “everything” spices and filled with cream cheese. The chef, Carmen Quagliata, is baking big, well-burnished gougères stuffed with eggs or spinach, eggs and ham, and bronzing chickens on the rotisserie. Sandwiches are also sold, and the beverages include wine, beer and cider, though it’s open only until 6 p.m.: 103 East 19th Street, 212-488-1505, dailyprovisionsnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/dining/08OFF/08OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/08/dining/08OFF/08OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/dining/08OFF/08OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/dining/08OFF/08OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/08/dining/08OFF/08OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight'