tml', 'snippet': 'Canada has rejected more than 72,000 applications from people seeking Indian status, the latest turn in a chaotic process to decide who in Newfoundland qualifies as a Native Canadian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Canada moved this week to revoke the Indian status of thousands of people in Newfoundland who had been recognized as “founding members” of the Qalipu First Nation band. It is the latest step in a chaotic process to decide who among the sprawling island’s nearly 530,000 people should be recognized as Native Canadians.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Apply, Few Qualify: Canada Rejects Indian Status for Thousands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newfoundland (Canada)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-08T02:50:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Canada', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig S. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54278c9c-b514-5aba-8663-0a528f813e28', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54278c9c-b514-5aba-8663-0a528f813e28'}, {'abstract': 'Ned White drops by.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/07/crosswords/opening-at-the-post-office-kelloggs-remington-picnic.html', 'snippet': 'Ned White drops by.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY PUZZLE — The middle of our solving week is when you can start to expect some real tricks in the puzzle. Clues become vaguer and start to play with words; themes become trickier and take more work to suss out.'