mbrace the part of myself I had deliberately ignored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One night when I was very young, I lay in my bed across from my older sister’s and described what I planned to look like when I grew up. My wavy brown hair would be straight and blond. My eyes, now the color of oversteeped tea, would turn blue. I wore a leg brace to bed in those days, a metal rod that buckled with a leather strap below my knee and attached to an ankle-high shoe. Though I felt the weight of this contraption as I spoke, and I knew I limped because the meanest girl on our block had told me, it went without saying that the beautiful future me would walk, and even run, with grace.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08disability/08disability-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love, Eventually', 'kicker': 'Disability', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love, Eventually', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cerebral Palsy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-08T08:20:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ona Gritz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gritz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/12b19429-8c30-5d5b-a319-7f3c57b0cd63', 'word_count': 1531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12b19429-8c30-5d5b-a319-7f3c57b0cd63'}, {'abstract': 'It’s increasingly evident that they have no workable plan and might never come up with one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/08/opinion/republicans-have-lost-the-plot-on-their-obamacare-repeal.html', 'snippet': 'It’s increasingly evident that they have no workable plan and might never come up with one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump and Republican lawmakers have never been able to explain how they would improve on the Affordable Care Act, which they’ve promised to quickly repeal and replace with something better. Now, it’s increasingly evident that they have no workable plan and might never come up with one.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08wed1/08wed1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1600, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Have Lost the Plot on Their Obamacare Repeal', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obamacare Repeal Hits a Brick Wall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-08T08:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/11539e12-fbb3-5a48-a64c-6823b64b5f21', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11539e12-fbb3-5a48-a64c-6823b64b5f21'}, {'abstract': 'Our cause is not partisan. It is to defend the pursuit of science, truth and freedom of thought.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/08/opinion/american-universities-must-take-a-stand.html', 'snippet': 'Our cause is not partisan. It is to defend the pursuit of science, truth and freedom of thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not since the era of witch hunts and “red baiting” has the American university faced so great a threat from government. How is the university to function when a president’s administration blurs the distinction between fact and fiction by asserting the existence of “alternative facts”? How can the university turn a blind eye to what every historian knows to be a key instrument of modern authoritarian regimes: the capacity to dress falsehood up as truth and reject the fruits of reasoned argument, evidence and rigorous verification?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08botstein/08botstein-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'American Universities Must Take a Stand', 'kicker': 'On Campus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'American Universities Must Take a Stand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACADEMIC FREEDOM', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-08T08:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leon Botstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bca876c0-16a0-5fab-b4e2-a2d78be004c2', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bca876c0-16a0-5fab-b4e2-a2d78be004c2'}, {'abstract': 'When students explore foreign cultures, they learn not just about others, but also about themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/08/opinion/preparing-young-americans-for-a-complex-world.html', 'snippet': 'When students explore foreign cultures, they learn not just about others, but also about themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, the Council on Foreign Relations and National Geographic commissioned a survey to assess the global literacy of American college students. Over 1,200 people participated; less than 30 percent earned a passing grade. Below are six questions they included, each of which a majority of respondents answered incorrectly. See how you, or your students or children, do. (Answers below.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preparing Young Americans for a Complex World', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dewitt Clinton High School', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teachers College of Columbia University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-08T08:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c054c0-f8ed-50da-aa4d-d4f3d6da3b5d', 'word_count': 1569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c054c0-f8ed-50da-aa4d-d4f3d6da3b5d'}, {'abstract': 'Trump made a series of reckless, unconnected promises to get elected, and now he’s just checking off each one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/08/opinion/connecting-trumps-dots.html', 'snippet': 'Trump made a series of reckless, unconnected promises to get elected, and now he’s just checking off each one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, the president’s behavior becomes more worrying. One day he demeans a federal judge who challenges him; the next day, without evidence, he accuses the media of hiding illegal voting or acts of terrorism. His lack of respect for institutions and truth pours out so fast, you start to forget how crazy this behavior is for any adult, let alone a president, and just how ugly things will get when we have a real crisis. And crises are baked into this story because of the incoherence of President Trump’s worldview.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08friedmanWeb/08friedmanWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1270, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Connecting Trump’s Dots', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Connecting Trump’s Dots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-08T08:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfd1e930-1c77-5026-88f1-bb5308713876', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfd1e930-1c77-5026-88f1-bb5308713876'}, {'abstract': 'Our idea would reduce carbon emissions, limit regulatory intrusion, promote economic growth and help working-class Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/08/opinion/a-conservative-case-for-climate-action.html', 'snippet': 'Our idea would reduce carbon emissions, limit regulatory intrusion, promote economic growth and help working-class Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CRAZY as it may sound, this is the perfect time to enact a sensible policy to address the dangerous threat of climate change. Before you call us nuts, hear us out.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08feldsteinWeb/08schulzWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/08/opinion/08feldsteinWeb/08schulzWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'x