nge soundscapes of an early electronic musician came with a whole philosophy of listening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Artistic innovations spurred by curiosity rather than by intellectual principles arguably produce more compelling and enduring breakthroughs. And Pauline Oliveros was undeniably curious when it came to music. By the time she was 9, she picked up the accordion; soon, she learned to play the tuba and the French horn. She quickly proved to be a highly versatile and accomplished instrumentalist. The capacity that really shaped Oliveros’s career as an experimental composer and electronic-music pioneer, however, was not her skill as a musician per se but her awareness of the broader sonic field that surrounded her as she played.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12lor/12lor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 1983, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: The Recordings of Pauline Oliveros', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Recordings of Pauline Oliveros', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ears and Hearing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliveros, Pauline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-09T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire-Louise Bennett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire-louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce4dc0be-7e1b-5a81-a1d5-0c4e72903dae', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce4dc0be-7e1b-5a81-a1d5-0c4e72903dae'}, {'abstract': 'Express your affection at home with a simple dish of chicken confit and roasted potatoes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/09/magazine/table-for-two-no-waiting.html', 'snippet': 'Express your affection at home with a simple dish of chicken confit and roasted potatoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Valentine’s Day is no time to take your lover out to dinner. Whatever scene you’ve conjured in your head for the evening — frisky conversation, a spray of roses, the way the tea lights on the restaurant table illuminate the face across from you — it’s probably going to remain a fiction. “Valentine’s Day is always such a weird vibe in the dining room,” the Los Angeles chef and restaurateur Jon Shook (Animal, Son of a Gun and Jon & Vinny’s, among others) told me. Everyone is anxious, even the staff. Amanda Cohen, the chef and owner of Dirt Candy in New York City, said she trains her servers to be extra alert. “Every table is a potential hurt locker,” she said, “each one of them an emotional bomb that might go off if jostled the wrong way.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/magazine/12eat-copy/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1565, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Table for T