'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brock Collection (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-09T22:49:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e560fa-32f4-5855-8ab4-ab53a49e4422', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e560fa-32f4-5855-8ab4-ab53a49e4422'}, {'abstract': "Donald Trump had a fine relationship with “Saturday Night Live” for nearly 30 years. That changed when Alec Baldwin, who will host Saturday's episode, started playing him.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/09/arts/television/donald-trump-saturday-night-live-alec-baldwin.html', 'snippet': "Donald Trump had a fine relationship with “Saturday Night Live” for nearly 30 years. That changed when Alec Baldwin, who will host Saturday's episode, started playing him.", 'lead_paragraph': 'For the 42 seasons that “Saturday Night Live” has been on the air, critiquing the show has not only been the preoccupation of comedy nerds but also every American’s national duty. No viewer, however, has seen his criticism of the show scrutinized — or had the show get under his skin — quite like President Trump. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/arts/trumpbaldwin/trumpbaldwin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/10/arts/trumpbaldwin/trumpbaldwin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/arts/trumpbaldwin/trumpbaldwin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_n