gether and drive wedges between the Republicans and President Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/opinion/a-game-plan-for-senate-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s how to drag your feet, stick together and drive wedges between the Republicans and President Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican majority in Washington has vowed to bulldoze the legacy of President Barack Obama. Because Democrats — despite round-the-clock efforts this week in the confirmation votes of Betsy DeVos as education secretary and Jeff Sessions as attorney general — have yet to block any member of President Trump’s cabinet, Democrats might appear to have little hope of stopping the Republican juggernaut.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10binderWeb/10binderWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Game Plan for Senate Democrats', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Game Plan for Senate Democrats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T08:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Binder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Binder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9b33b46-4c4e-5e95-aa53-83ebbf1b4303', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9b33b46-4c4e-5e95-aa53-83ebbf1b4303'}, {'abstract': 'Elena Filip is one of tens of thousands of Romanians who have taken to the icy, cold streets of Bucharest to demand government accountability. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/world/europe/romania-bucharest-corruption-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Elena Filip is one of tens of thousands of Romanians who have taken to the icy, cold streets of Bucharest to demand government accountability. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the ninth straight day, Elena Filip bundled up in her fur-trimmed ski suit and left her Bucharest apartment for Piata Victoriei — Victory Square — outside the government headquarters. She was off to join thousands of other Romanians angry about the government’s recent decision to effectively allow official corruption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Want a Better Life in a Better Country’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Romania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T08:22:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Megan Specia and Yara Bishara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Specia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Yara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7746a24-3b66-5f8f-90b7-0df52b98714c', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7746a24-3b66-5f8f-90b7-0df52b98714c'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump has promised to rid America of the immigrant threat. But Guadalupe García de Rayos was a threat to no one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/opinion/bad-dude-no-but-deported-anyway.html', 'snippet': 'President Trump has promised to rid America of the immigrant threat. But Guadalupe García de Rayos was a threat to no one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By no standard of common sense or decency should Guadalupe García de Rayos have been a priority for deportation. Ms. Rayos, a 35-year-old mother of two, was arrested on Wednesday by Immigration and Customs Enforcement agents in Phoenix. On Thursday she was deported to Mexico, a country she left 21 years ago. Her devastated family, including her American-born children, remains in the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/opinion/10fri1/10fri1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1884, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bad Dude’? No, but Deported Anyway', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Bad Dude’? No, but Deported Anyway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T08:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b8dbbbe-bddf-5fcc-a1c7-ea82ba48ec3e', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b8dbbbe-bddf-5fcc-a1c7-ea82ba48ec3e'}, {'abstract': 'Andre Wagner, a photographer based in Brooklyn, roamed the streets of Manhattan this winter in search of stylish moments. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/fashion/new-york-city-street-photography.html', 'snippet': 'Andre Wagner, a photographer based in Brooklyn, roamed the streets of Manhattan this winter in search of stylish moments. ', 'lead_paragraph': '“It might be cold, but the city streets are still filled with culture and discovery if you’re open to it,” said Andre Wagner, a photographer based in Brooklyn, who roamed the streets of Manhattan this winter in search of stylish moments. “The goal for me is to always try and make photographs that are more beautiful than what was photographed.”  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/29/fashion/29THELOOK1-WEB/29THELOOK1-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width':