adline': {'main': 'Todd Rovak on Turning Tough Days Into Good Ones', 'kicker': 'Corner Office', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turning Tough Days Into Good Ones', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rovak, Todd H (1978- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fahrenheit 212 LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cap Gemini SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T12:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Bryant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/279e09ef-a993-5894-932a-5c8759dcb4bc', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279e09ef-a993-5894-932a-5c8759dcb4bc'}, {'abstract': 'Behind the scenes, female executives and visual effects experts have been working to bring gender equity to a specialty field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/movies/star-wars-women-visual-effects.html', 'snippet': 'Behind the scenes, female executives and visual effects experts have been working to bring gender equity to a specialty field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jyn Erso is not a princess or a Jedi. She is, however, the second female character with a lead role in a “Star Wars” movie in the last two years. It’s a statistic that would have been unthinkable 40 years ago, when Princess Leia reigned alone in a galaxy of men and her dialogue was less than half that of the golden droid C-3PO in “A New Hope.” But even with the advent of back-to-back female protagonists, the women onscreen are only now catching up with those working behind the scenes at Industrial Light & Magic, the special-effects studio founded by George Lucas.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12STARWARSWOMEN1/12STARWARSWOMEN1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Women of ‘Star Wars.’ (It’s Not Who You Think.)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Women Behind the Force', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Industrial Light and Magic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lucasfilm Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, Lynwen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Kathleen (1953- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T12:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathalia Holt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c335459-ffe9-52ac-9060-60acd9d40660', 'word_count': 1308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c335459-ffe9-52ac-9060-60acd9d40660'}, {'abstract': 'Amid the furor over the new education secretary, the reality is that the federal government has limited influence over the city’s schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/nyregion/betsy-devos-education-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Amid the furor over the new education secretary, the reality is that the federal government has limited influence over the city’s schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, the day the Senate confirmed Betsy DeVos as education secretary with an unprecedented tiebreaking vote from the vice president, hundreds of high school students in New York City left their classrooms and convened downtown in Foley Square to protest the presidency of Donald J. Trump, both for his immigration policies and for whatever his Republican administration might do to the nation’s public school system. Antipathies toward Ms. DeVos ran high. “We love public school,” the students chanted. “Betsy DeVos is a fool.” It is hard to think of the last time an enormous group of teenagers would have been able to name the education secretary, let alone generate such impassioned feeling for whomever held the post.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/nyregion/12BIG1-SUB/12BIG1-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaction in New York to Betsy DeVos? A Lot of Shrugs', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reaction to Trump’s Education Chief? In the City, a Lot of 