director and forever cool girl takes T on a tour of Darien, Conn., from her middle school to the “iconic teen hangout” (a Mobil station).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-home-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'The actress, director and forever cool girl takes T on a tour of Darien, Conn., from her middle school to the “iconic teen hangout” (a Mobil station).', 'lead_paragraph': 'As childhoods go, Chloë Sevigny’s in Darien, Conn., a wealthy town of 20,000 an hour’s train ride from New York City, was as suburban as they come: There was sledding and softball practice and long days spent playing outside with neighbor kids on the cul-de-sac where she lived, until the third grade, with her parents and older brother, Paul. “My mom would open the door in the morning, and we wouldn’t come back until the night. It was all about being outside,” Sevigny, who has been living in Brooklyn since 2013, says when we meet in Darien on a 27-degree day in December. The house, she remembers, had a big forsythia bush in the front yard. “It was, like, my spot,” she says, as we drive past gracious colonial-style homes with manicured lawns. “I always just chilled there, underneath. It was all very, you know ...” She begins to laugh, a boisterous, asthmatic-sounding, from-the-gut guffaw that signals she’s aware of the triteness, the irony or maybe just the sheer unlikeliness of what she’s about to say: “... idyllic.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '180', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/10/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A/chloe-sevigny-slide-Z29A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1300, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Home With Chloë Sevigny', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chloë of Connecticut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sevigny, Chloe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Darien (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T14:50:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Fortini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fortini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 