r maximum returns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saving money in a 529 plan offers families a way to put cash away for college and save on taxes as well. But if your child is entering high school soon, it’s time to double-check the allocation of your investments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Manage a 529 Plan for Your Child’s Education', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Manage a 529 Plan for Your Child’s Education', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T16:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/953f511e-266e-5bb6-aeb5-bfb0d41ddb10', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953f511e-266e-5bb6-aeb5-bfb0d41ddb10'}, {'abstract': 'Little evidence supports a longstanding legend of alligators living in the New York sewer system, but that doesn’t dissuade Manhattan’s historian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/nyregion/gators-in-the-sewer-i-want-it-to-be-true.html', 'snippet': 'Little evidence supports a longstanding legend of alligators living in the New York sewer system, but that doesn’t dissuade Manhattan’s historian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City may have been blanketed with a snowstorm on Thursday, but under those snow-strewn streets, legions of