ument_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEETI UPADHYE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neeti', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'UPADHYE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a1b91652-3b09-5265-a2a2-a7cbde44240d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a1b91652-3b09-5265-a2a2-a7cbde44240d'}, {'abstract': 'A Ballet de Lorraine program at the Joyce Theater hides the identities of its featured dance makers — a thrilling premise that ultimately disappoints.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/arts/dance/ballet-de-lorraine-unknown-pleasures-joyce-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'A Ballet de Lorraine program at the Joyce Theater hides the identities of its featured dance makers — a thrilling premise that ultimately disappoints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you look at a dance work differently if you don’t know who made it? A choreographer’s name, like that of any artist, is a brand — a repository for reputation, necessary for fandom and crucial for marketing. But that same reputation can become a trap, compelling an artist to deliver the familiar and a viewer to expect it, with preconceptions and prejudices that can obscure the work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/arts/11LORRAINE1/11LORRAINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Unknown Pleasures’ Makes Unfulfilled Promises', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet de Lorraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T23:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1941c231-8287-502c-8982-037e3dc298cc', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1941c231-8287-502c-8982-037e3dc298cc'}, {'abstract': 'The label celebrates its 15th birthday with an exhibition of portraits shot on a vintage Polaroid, the sitters in the new fall collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/fashion/marcus-wainwright-rag-and-bone-photography-show-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'The label celebrates its 15th birthday with an exhibition of portraits shot on a vintage Polaroid, the sitters in the new fall collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marcus Wainwright, the chief executive and creative director of Rag & Bone, sat in his 13th Street Rag & Bone studio, converted for two days into two makeshift photo studios to shoot 74 portraits, with all of the chaos and confusion that entailed. At one side, the photographer Glen Luchford worked a Polaroid camera the size of a small car that churns out 20-inch-by-24-inch instant photos on ancient, rapidly expiring, no-longer-in-production film. At another, Frank Lebon coaxed his subjects into bouncing on trampolines as he shot them on film and an iPhone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/fashion/11RAGBONE3/11RAGBONE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rag & Bone Says No to the Runway Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Rag &amp; Bone, the Runway Show Is History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rag & Bone (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wainwright, Marcus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-10T23:26:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a37d32d2-559f-5b72-bf6b-c074745c0c5b', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a37d32d2-559f-5b72-bf6b-c074745c0c5b'}, {'abstract': 'A New York City Ballet principal, Mr. Huxley carries the refined and poetic air of a silent-movie star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/10/arts/dance/anthony-huxley-new-york-city-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'A New York City Ballet principal, Mr. Huxley carries the refined and poetic air of a silent-movie star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In dance, “voice” can refer to the way a body moves, not just the words that come from it. It has taken Anthony Huxley, shy by nature, time to find both. For years, he rarely spoke. He could hide behind his impeccable technique. It’s almost as if a classical step, beautifully executed, became a kind of armor used to shield himself from the world.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 877}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 701, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/arts/12HUXLEY1/12HUXLEY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1401, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Huxley, the Anti-Jock of City Ballet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline