': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Expedia Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-11T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo and Mike Isaac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db95c7da-4f29-537b-8d1b-25ee6cc76827', 'word_count': 1010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db95c7da-4f29-537b-8d1b-25ee6cc76827'}, {'abstract': 'The building next door is so brightly lit, it’s as if the sun is shining into my bedroom at midnight. Is that legal?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/11/realestate/are-there-laws-to-limit-excessive-light.html', 'snippet': 'The building next door is so brightly lit, it’s as if the sun is shining into my bedroom at midnight. Is that legal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I live in a small walk-up in Park Slope, Brooklyn. My bedroom windows face a six-story condominium. Those  windows are about 50 feet from six floor-to-ceiling glass walls in front of hallways. The building keeps fluorescent lights on in all six hallways all night long, creating a 60-foot-tall wall of light bright enough to make it look like the sun is shining into my bedroom at midnight. I hung light-blocking curtains and put black construction paper in my windows, which make the room dark enough to sleep. But is it legal for a building to create such an excessive amount of light pollution?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 102, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 102}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 174, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Are There Laws to Limit Excessive Light?', 'kicker': 'Ask Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Does Any Regulation Limit the Light Coming From an Adjacent Building?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biorhythms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-11T15:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronda Kaysen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaysen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7da0840-4512-5e51-8366-df52234805da', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7da0840-4512-5e51-8366-df52234805da'}, {'abstract': 'The makeup team shared a single tube of Maybelline Great Lash in Royal Blue — a cult-favorite, discontinued shade that will be reintroduced in May.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/11/t-magazine/fashion/jason-wu-blue-mascara-beauty-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'The makeup team shared a single tube of Maybelline Great Lash in Royal Blue — a cult-favorite, discontinued shade that will be reintroduced in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the bright orange-red lip at Jason Wu’s fall/winter 2017 presentation was full of high-impact energy, it wasn’t the most compelling part of the beauty look. Instead, a subtle — but significant — flick of cobalt mascara generated quite a commotion backstage. “It’s a bit of Great Lash in Royal Blue,” said the makeup artist Yadim, name-checking the cult-classic shade that Maybelline discontinued in 2014 and makeup obsessives have been tracking ever since. Its appearance in Yadim’s kit, however, confirmed that the brand will, in fact, release it again: It will hit shelves this spring (May, to be exact).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/t-magazine/fashion/11tmag-bbr