 $30 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/11/business/miles-cahn-dead-coach.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cahn founded the company with his wife, Lillian, in New York City in 1961. They sold the upscale handbag business in 1985 for a reported $30 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Miles Cahn, who with his wife founded the Coach Leatherware Company, which helped redefine the American handbag as both chic and practical, died on Friday at his home in Manhattan. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/obituaries/12cahn-obit/12cahn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/12/obituaries/12cahn-obit/12cahn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/obituaries/12cahn-obit/12cahn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 458, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/12/obituaries/12cahn-obit/12cahn-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 458, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Miles Cahn, Co-Founder of Coach Handbags, Dies at 95', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Miles Cahn, 95, a Coach Founder; Helped Make Handbags Practical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahn, Miles (1921-2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coach Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cahn, Lillian (1923-2013)', 'rank'