ings.html', 'snippet': 'Fleeing an arranged marriage, the couple were shot to death by family members in what is often called an honor killing. There have been no arrests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — An armed mob that included relatives of a young woman who had eloped with her lover stormed a police station holding the couple in eastern Afghanistan over the weekend, then dragged the lovers off and killed them, officials and witnesses said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mob Kills Eloped Lovers After Storming Afghan Police Station', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mob Kills Eloped Lovers After Storming a Police Station in Eastern Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Honor Killings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nuristan Province (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-13T18:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zahra Nader and Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zahra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nader', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/028d24b0-c1ec-58f8-9d8c-b7d5ca5230fc', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/028d24b0-c1ec-58f8-9d8c-b7d5ca5230fc'}, {'abstract': 'Nigeria’s president, Muhammadu Buhari, was receiving medical treatment in London, but his aides have disclosed few details.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/13/world/africa/muhammadu-buha