: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62dc3205-638d-540a-ba91-5982d4dc588e', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62dc3205-638d-540a-ba91-5982d4dc588e'}, {'abstract': 'A new line of dips from the California brand Heidi’s Salsa goes from zero to spicy hot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/13/dining/salsa-california-heidis.html', 'snippet': 'A new line of dips from the California brand Heidi’s Salsa goes from zero to spicy hot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heidi’s Salsa, from California, sells three versions of the chunky tomato dip that are hard to distinguish from appearance alone. On the palate, they tell a different story. The Original Mild, based on a family recipe, is just that, with a modest kick in the finish and a texture that would welcome pasta as well as tacos. The Happy Medium is almost as forceful as the hot Chupacabra’s Revenge, which also has more complexity: Heidi’s Salsa, $12 for two, $18 for three 16-ounce jars, heidissalsa.com; also sold at Target stores and in New York City at Morton Williams.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15BURNER-SALSA/15BURNER-SALSA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15BURNER-SALSA/15BURNER-SALSA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15BURNER-SALSA/15BURNER-SALSA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/