rticleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/11/opinion/11sat2web/11sat2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/opinion/11sat2web/11sat2web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/11/opinion/11sat2web/11sat2web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michael Flynn’s Phone Call With Russia', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phone Call With Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flynn, Michael T', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-13T19:51:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/40aa2622-bf6a-5717-973c-410c2a12d5a3', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40aa2622-bf6a-5717-973c-410c2a12d5a3'}, {'abstract': 'Mary Stephenson tackles real-life singledom with a playful approach to relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/mary-stephenson-man-clay.html', 'snippet': 'Mary Stephenson tackles real-life singledom with a playful approach to relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a wedding once,\xa0the\xa0artist Mary Stephenson\xa0explained to another guest that she had been single for years.\xa0“What a waste,”\xa0was the stranger’s reply. And just like that, Stephenson\xa0was inspired to create her\xa0irreverent\xa0“My Man”\xa0series.\xa0Far from being a rage against spinsterhood,\xa0her\xa0lighthearted series\xa0consists of works of similar construction: Stephenson photographed alongside the\xa0“boyfriends” she creates, against painterly tableaus\xa0of romantic settings. “This is a playful way of acting out my anticipated relationships rather than just internalizing them,”\xa0the 28-year-old\xa0explains from her studio in Dalston, East London, which resembles the backstage of a theater\xa0thanks to piles of props, costumes and scenery.\xa0', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/13/t-magazine/art/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN/13tmag-boyfriends-slide-EJFN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Artist Making — and Dating — Clay Men', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Matters; ‘Boyfriends’ as Life like Props, but Passive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-13T19:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aae5cbff-15ed-5898-8ee3-62140987d74a', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aae5cbff-15ed-5898-8ee3-62140987d74a'}, {'abstract': 'How does the pontiff in the HBO series compare with the real-life one? The Rome bureau chief calls it this way: Truth is stranger than fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/13/arts/television/you-may-be-the-young-pope-but-youre-no-francis.html', 'snippet': 'How does the pontiff in the HBO series compare with the real-life one? The Rome bureau chief calls it this way: Truth is stranger than fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HBO’s “The Young Pope” depicts the dashing and fictitious Pope Pius XIII as a ruthless knife fighter willing to cut down anyone in his path back to a purer church. Yet as I binge-wa