spacious, casual space from Dale Talde and his partners, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRE MEZCALERIA The spotlight is back on Denisse Lina Chavez, the chef and a partner at El Atoradero, who withdrew from the kitchen in the fall after an injury. She is recovering, and she’s back. And not only is she cooking her home-style Mexican fare at the restaurant, where she will be adding some new tacos and other dishes, but she is also making food for Madre Mezcaleria, a new bar next door specializing in mezcals, which she opened with her partner, Noah Arenstein. Light food like oysters, ceviches and tostadas are central to the bar’s menu. The space, with a dozen seats at the bar and a banquette with tables, includes talavera tiles that Ms. Chavez brought back from Mexico: 706 Washington Avenue (Prospect Place), Prospect Heights, Brooklyn, 718-399-0706.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'