name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By MAX BERLINGER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Max', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BERLINGER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6a04dcc2-228e-5e41-925e-9fcca66b332d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6a04dcc2-228e-5e41-925e-9fcca66b332d'}, {'abstract': 'Three parties were held on Monday, hosted by Olivier Zahm at Narcissa, Philipp Plein at the New York Public Library and Humberto Leon at Mission Chinese.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/14/fashion/purple-magazine-philipp-plein-opening-ceremony-founder-party-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'Three parties were held on Monday, hosted by Olivier Zahm at Narcissa, Philipp Plein at the New York Public Library and Humberto Leon at Mission Chinese.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A trio of parties on Monday night demonstrated how diverse the fashion week social scene can be. First, Purple magazine held its customary dinner at the Standard, East Village, a familial gathering of veteran scenesters overseen by Olivier Zahm, the magazine’s editor and nightlife consigliere. Then Philipp Plein hosted an extravagant affair at the New York Public Library, with a V.I.P. dinner upstairs and a bigger party downstairs. And Humberto Leon of Opening Ceremony teamed with photographer Ryan McGinley for a one-night revival of B.East, a popular gay party, at its former location on East Broadway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Purple Magazine, Philipp Plein and Opening Ceremony Founder Party on Monday Night of Fashion Week', 'kicker': 'Party Coverage: Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philipp Plein (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opening Ceremony LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-14T22:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Max Berlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Max', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a362ecf-6d83-5e35-bd83-d8b7e40d4abb', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a362ecf-6d83-5e35-bd83-d8b7e40d4abb'}, {'abstract': 'At Coach, Guido Palau enhanced each model’s natural beauty rather than creating a cookie-cutter hairstyle. Here’s how he recommends styling yours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/coach-hair-texture-beauty-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'At Coach, Guido Palau enhanced each model’s natural beauty rather than creating a cookie-cutter hairstyle. Here’s how he recommends styling yours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent seasons, many designers have made a strong appeal for women to feel comfortable in their own skin — starting with their hair. “As a trend, it seems like lots of designers are embracing all the different kinds of girls they book by enhancing their natural beauty. So that’s what we’ve done at Coach,” noted Guido Palau, Redken’s global creative director and the lead stylist responsible for creating the individually textured hair looks on the diverse cast of models at today’s Coach show. Unlike the toughened-up, greasy-slick locks created to match last spring’s rock ’n’ roll-themed collection, Palau explained that the current style spoke more to the spirit of the fall/winter 2017 collection than its actual aesthetic: cool, easy and eclectic, he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-bbr01/14tmag-bbr01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Play Up This Season’s Best Hair Texture: Your Own', 'kicker': 'Backstage Beauty Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'sub