iticism of him, no matter how benign, with vitriol. She now says she “hates” all liberals, all Democrats and, particularly, Barack Obama.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 865}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 710, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 938, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/magazine/19ethicist/19mag-19ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s a Liberal to Do When His Spouse Is a Trump Zealot?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Wife Is a Trump Zealot. What’s a Liberal to Do?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-15T10:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b43c3d30-3b9f-5cf2-93c2-9020668aa0af', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b43c3d30-3b9f-5cf2-93c2-9020668aa0af'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate panel has, at least for the moment, chief responsibility for getting to the bottom of events surrounding the resignation of Michael T. Flynn and any foreign meddling in the 2016 election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/15/us/politics/pressure-on-senate-intelligence-committee-to-deliver-on-russia-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate panel has, at least for the moment, chief responsibility for getting to the bottom of events surrounding the resignation of Michael T. Flynn and any foreign meddling in the 2016 election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It does most of its work in secret, can be highly partisan and its members consider it a thankless job with few political benefits. But the Senate Intelligence Committee is suddenly central to a capital increasingly rattled by Trump administration turmoil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':