idants of Mr. Kim who later became targets of his displeasure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/15/world/asia/north-korea-executions-kim-jong-un.html', 'snippet': 'The list of executions and purges is punctuated with the names of high-ranking officials and confidants of Mr. Kim who later became targets of his displeasure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — After Kim Jong-un’s half brother, Kim Jong-nam, was killed in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, South Korean officials were quick to blame the North Korean leader. It would not be the first time that someone who has fallen out of favor with Kim Jong-un has been targeted in either a purge or an outright execution. A South Korean think tank, the Institute for National Security Strategy, released a report recently saying that Mr. Kim had ordered the executions of 340 people since coming to power in 2011. Some who fall out of favor are not killed but are abruptly stripped of power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/world/16purge-1/16purge-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For North Koreans in Kim Jong-un’s Orbit, Falling From Favor Can Be Deadly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falling From Favor Can Be Deadly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jang Song-Thaek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Won-hong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Yong-jin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-15T11:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6196bd9a-ca41-54c5-956f-44666d7a2e60', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6196bd9a-ca41-54c5-956f-44666d7a2e60'}, {'abstract': 'This novel follows an estranged wife’s journey to Greece in search of her missing husband.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/15/books/review/separation-katie-kitamura.html', 'snippet': 'This novel follows an estranged wife’s journey to Greece in search of her missing husband.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SEPA