l': 'By LENA DUNHAM', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DUNHAM', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/07ab6f7f-2f33-5c7b-a065-b490e0ea7008', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/07ab6f7f-2f33-5c7b-a065-b490e0ea7008'}, {'abstract': 'The Christian governor of the Indonesian capital, who has been charged with blaspheming Islam, finished first in voting this week. But the second round may be another story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/16/world/asia/jakarta-governor-election.html', 'snippet': 'The Christian governor of the Indonesian capital, who has been charged with blaspheming Islam, finished first in voting this week. But the second round may be another story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — This week’s bitterly contested election for governor of Jakarta — pitting a Christian incumbent charged with blaspheming Islam against two rivals who emphasized their Muslim faith — was widely seen as a test of whether Indonesia’s young democracy could resist the pull of sectarian politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/world/17indonesia-1/17indonesia-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/17/world/17indonesia-1/17indonesia-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/world/17indonesia-1/17indonesia-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/world/17indonesia-1/1