. The director Gore Verbinski explains in the video and in excerpts below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gore Verbinski Narrates a Scene From ‘A Cure for Wellness’', 'kicker': 'Anatomy of a Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verbinski, Gore', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeHaan, Dane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Cure for Wellness (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-16T20:31:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84e741aa-a77a-5bd1-9725-0f0a978521ea', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84e741aa-a77a-5bd1-9725-0f0a978521ea'}, {'abstract': "Newly discovered black-and-white footage of a 1904 wedding filmed shows a glimpse of a young man with a mustache, wearing a bowler hat and formal suit, descending a flight of stairs (about 4 seconds into the footage). It's believed to be the only existing film of the French writer.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/europe/100000004937650/found-the-only-known-footage-of-proust.html', 'snippet': "Newly discovered black-and-white footage of a 1904 wedding filmed shows a glimpse of a young man with a mustache, wearing a bowler hat and formal suit, descending a flight of stairs (about 4 seconds into the footage). It's believed to be the only ...", 'lead_paragraph': "Newly discovered black-and-white footage of a 1904 wedding filmed shows a glimpse of a young man with a mustache, wearing a bowler hat a