ganizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trian Fund Management LP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gillette Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, David S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-16T21:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Silva Laughlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': 'Silva', 'lastname': 'Laughlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b83e3227-295b-50d3-a91d-b02ab0620940', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b83e3227-295b-50d3-a91d-b02ab0620940'}, {'abstract': 'Zhang Yimou’s costume spectacle offers drooling creatures, glowering warriors, a swaggering mercenary and a message about China’s might.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/16/movies/the-great-wall-review-matt-damon.html', 'snippet': 'Zhang Yimou’s costume spectacle offers drooling creatures, glowering warriors, a swaggering mercenary and a message about China’s might.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Snarling digital monsters, a glowering Matt Damon and battalions of unfaltering Chinese warriors mix it up in “The Great Wall,” a painless, overstuffed spectacle that works overtime as a testament to China’s might. Set once upon a time, the movie spins a legend that never was: Every 60 years, slavering creatures emerge from beyond to sharpen their teeth on human bones and stuff their bellies on meat. The whole thing plays out as if it had been thought up by someone who, while watching “Game of Thrones” and smoking a bowl, started riffing on walls, China and production money.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 's