erplate dialogue. Mr. Franco stars and directs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Franco’s screen adaptation of John Steinbeck’s 1936 novel, “In Dubious Battle,” about striking California fruit pickers, is the farthest thing imaginable from the titillating provocations for which Mr. Franco is notorious. Along with his films based on William Faulkner’s “As I Lay Dying” and “The Sound and the Fury,” it belongs to the literary subgenre that might be called James Franco’s eat-your-spinach movies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/17/arts/17INDUBIOUS/17INDUBIOUS-superJumbo-v3.jpg',