n Britain, the country he led for a decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tony Blair Wants ‘Brexit’ Opponents to ‘Rise Up.’ But Will Anyone Listen?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blair Urges ‘Brexit’ Foes to ‘Rise Up’ Before It’s Too Late', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Great Britain Withdrawal from EU (Brexit)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Theresa M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-17T15:20:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c35c12d-f22d-579f-a528-8076b4b9de25', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c35c12d-f22d-579f-a528-8076b4b9de25'}, {'abstract': 'The illustrations of Santiago Ramón y Cajal, the father of modern neuroscience, are featured in the new book “The Beautiful Brain.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/17/science/santiago-ramon-y-cajal-beautiful-brain.html', 'snippet': 'The illustrations of Santiago Ramón y Cajal, the father of modern neuroscience, are featured in the new book “The Beautiful Brain.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some microscopes today are so powerful that they can\xa0create a picture of the gap between brain cells, which is thousands of times smaller than the width of a human hair. They can even reveal the tiny sacs\xa0carrying even tinier nuggets of information\xa0to cross over that gap\xa0to form memories. And in colorful\xa0snapshots\xa0made possible by a\xa0giant magnet, we can see the activity of close to 100 billion brain cells talking.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/16/science/cajal-comp/cajal-comp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hunched Over a Microscope, He Sketched the Secrets of How the Brain Works', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nerves and Nervous System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Beautiful Brain: The Drawings of Santiago Ramon y Cajal (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramon y Cajal, Santiago', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-17T15:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf0ad82-0280-555c-939a-369806e3de87', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf0ad82-0280-555c-939a-369806e3de87'}, {'abstract': 'The star of “The Blacklist: Redemption” talks about depicting powerful female characters and shares her thoughts on sexism in Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/17/arts/television/famke-janssen-plays-another-lethal-woman-in-a-blacklist-spinoff.html', 'snippet': 'The star of “The Blacklist: Redemption” talks about depicting powerful female characters and shares her thoughts on sexism in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Famke Janssen looks like a woman you wouldn’t want to tangle with: six statuesque feet crowned by intense wide-set eyes and cheekbones like granite outcroppings. She also acts like one, forging her career on damsels more likely to cause distress than to be mired in it. Now Ms. Janssen is striding — with the legs she used to crush men as a Bond girl in “GoldenEye” — into her first starring network role, on “The Blacklist: Redemption,” beginning Thursday, Feb. 23, on NBC.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The 