2/17/books/review/rush-of-blood-mark-billingha.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Billingham’s “Rush of Blood” is a savage satire about good friends whose special bond originated in murder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ugly Americans on a European vacation are always good for a laugh. But you laugh at your peril at the Ugly Brits vacationing in America in RUSH OF BLOOD (Atlantic Monthly, $25), Mark Billingham’s savage satire about good friends whose special bond originated in murder. Three couples who are all from London find themselves staying at the same cheesy beach resort on Siesta Key in Sarasota. That’s as good a reason as any for Angie and Barry, Dave and Marina, and Ed and Sue to strike up a friendship when they meet at the Pelican Palms.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/books/review/0219-BKS-Crime/0219-BKS-Crime-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/19/books/review/0219-BKS-Crime/0219-BKS-Crime-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 794}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/books/review/0219-BKS-Crime/0219-BKS-Crime-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 774, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/books/review/0219-BKS-Crime/0219-BKS-Crime-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 905, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/books/review/0219-BKS-Crime/0219-BKS-Crime-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': '