e': None, 'lastname': 'Tam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/569b6d8a-65b6-5723-b3da-31f0c7dd1ffd', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/569b6d8a-65b6-5723-b3da-31f0c7dd1ffd'}, {'abstract': 'Sheelah Kolhatkar, whose “Black Edge” traces the insider trading scandal at SAC Capital, is a former fund analyst herself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/17/books/review/she-began-her-career-at-hedge-funds-now-she-reports-on-their-crimes.html', 'snippet': 'Sheelah Kolhatkar, whose “Black Edge” traces the insider trading scandal at SAC Capital, is a former fund analyst herself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Other People’s Money: Before she became a journalist, the New Yorker staff writer Sheelah Kolhatkar worked in the late 1990s and early 2000s as an analyst at a couple of small hedge funds specializing in risk arbitrage — basically, she researched companies that planned to merge, and tried to predict how their stock prices would move. “I fell into hedge funds by accident,” she told me in a recent phone call about her new book, “Black Edge,” a look at the insider trading scandal that brought down the huge fund SAC Capital even as its founder escaped prosecution. (The book makes its debut on the hardcover nonfiction list at No.\u202f12.) Kolhatkar got her start in finance as a temp, answering phones, shortly after she graduated from Stanford with a master’s degree in media studies. “This was early in the evolution of hedge funds,” she said, “and a lot of them were willing to take a chance hiring the kind of people you might not expect. There was a start-up atmosphere, so everyone got to do a bit of everything. And the fund manager just sort of took a liking to me. She told me: ‘Look, your boyfriend is a filmmaker. One of you should make some money. I’m giving you an opportunity to learn the business and make some dough to keep living in New York City.’ So I took a crash course in financial analysis and investing. It was like learning a new language.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/books/review/26list-blackedge/26list-blackedge-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 256, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/books/review/26list-blackedge/26list-blackedge-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 256, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/books/review/26list-blackedge/26list-blackedge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/books/review/26list-blackedge/26list-blackedge-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/books/review/26list-blackedge/26list-blackedge-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'She Began Her Career at Hedge Funds. Now She Reports on Their Crimes.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Black Edge: Inside Information, Dirty Money, and the Quest to Bring Down the Most Wanted Man on Wall Street (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kolhatkar, Sheelah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-17T17:25:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e1a84e7-5384-51d8-a646-b3bd1174a148', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e1a84e7-5384-51d8-a646-b3bd1174a148'}, {'abstract': 'This is the Korean word for mask.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2017/02/17/well/korean_2_thal.html', 'snippet': 'This is the Korean word for mask.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the Korean word for mask.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Korean: 탈', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-02-17T17:27:42+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Well', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/cbe0e4fc-6740-5625-baf5-8f1e17ce01f2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/cbe0e4fc-6740-5625-baf5-8f1e17ce01f2'}, {'abstract': 'This is the Korean word for daughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2017/02/17/well/Korean_3_ttal.html', 'snippet': 'This is the Korean word for daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the Korean word for daughter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Korean: 딸', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-02-17T17:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Well', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/09d2502c-0896-582d-a5f9-ca78b77bbcaa