ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Watching', 'section_name': 'Watching', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Berman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6123decd-123a-587a-a631-6235fec8a6f6', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6123decd-123a-587a-a631-6235fec8a6f6'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s rambling, defiant performance in a televised session with the news media was unsettling for many international observers, but not all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/17/world/trump-news-conference-provokes-anxiety-humor-and-shrugs-around-world.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s rambling, defiant performance in a televised session with the news media was unsettling for many international observers, but not all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was no mention on Thursday of President Trump on Russia’s state television, which suddenly went silent about the American president after months of fawning coverage. At the BBC, a prominent host found himself facing down charges of fake news by a Trump aide. And in China, one sarcastic commenter predicted on social media that Mr. Trump might be a Communist Party agent who would bring down the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/18/world/18trump-reax/18trump-reax-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump News Conference Provokes Anxiety, Humor and Shrugs Around World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watching Trump From Abroad With Sarcasm, Silence and Scorn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-17T17:54:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d753aa0-e379-53fc-9070-04b32ae2dfd2', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d753aa0-e379-53fc-9070-04b32ae2dfd2'}, {'abstract': 'Sara Friedlander, head of Postwar and Contemporary Art in New York at Christie’s, makes her infant daughter a priority on Sundays, dressing her up and taking her to restaurants and museums.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/17/nyregion/sara-friedlander-sunday-routine.html', 'snippet': 'Sara Friedlander, head of Postwar and Contemporary Art in New York at Christie’s, makes her infant daughter a priority on Sundays, dressing her up and taking her to restaurants and museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Sara Friedlander, the head of Postwar and Contemporary Art at Christie’s in New York, weekdays often involve 14-hour days at the office, attending events and juggling her charity auctioneering jobs. So on Sundays, Ms. Friedlander’s 7-month-old, Helaina, called Lainie, is her top priority. Ms. Friedlander, 33, lives on the Upper West Side, where she grew up, with her husband, Matt Siegel, 33, chief digital officer for Roc Nation, the entertainment company of the singer Jay Z. SHIVANI VORA', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/nyregion/19ROUTINE1/19ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/19/nyregion/19ROUTINE1/19ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/nyregion/19ROUTINE1/19ROUTINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/19/nyregion/19ROUTINE1/19ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/19/nyregi