ally frozen for 30 years, the comic villain created by the actor Mike Myers is shocked when he is told that $1 million isn’t a lot of money in 1997.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 855}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26WEALTHCOVER/26WEALTHCOVER-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Are the Richest of the Rich?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Most Exclusive Club', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wealth-X Pte Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-19T05:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SpecialSections', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ac7a7b9-8315-5d54-ab39-d2fa62693cde', 'word_count': 2442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ac7a7b9-8315-5d54-ab39-d2fa62693cde'}, {'abstract': 'A look at 10 billionaires’ money reveals one thing the superrich have in common: a large amount of cash and liquid securities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/19/your-money/where-the-worlds-wealthiest-invest-their-billions.html', 'snippet': 'A look at 10 billionaires’ money reveals one thing the superrich have in common: a large amount of cash and liquid securities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Being part of the global billionaire class is beyond the imagination of most people. At the threshold of $1 billion, a 5 percent return would yield an annual interest payment of $50 million — without ever touching the principal. But how billionaires, from those in the single digits to near the top, invest shows a range of options for the very wealthiest in the world. One thing they all have in common is a large amount of money in cash or equivalently liquid securities. Here’s a look at how 10 billionaires have made and invested their money, according to public filings gathered by the financial research firm Wealth-X. ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/your-money/26DOSSIER-ARNAULT/26DOS