k': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Topshop', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-20T15:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8fd04135-58c4-5986-bc57-b6fbefa1255a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8fd04135-58c4-5986-bc57-b6fbefa1255a'}, {'abstract': 'The beauty look for Topshop Unique‘s fall/winter 2017 look was pure nostalgia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/20/t-magazine/topshop-unique-beauty-london-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'The beauty look for Topshop Unique‘s fall/winter 2017 look was pure nostalgia.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s about a beautiful urban explorer,” said the makeup artist Lynsey Alexander backstage at Topshop Unique’s fall/winter 2017 show. “She’s a girl who likes to have fun.” Taking Danny Boyle’s cinematic ode to hedonism — the 2000 film “The Beach” — as the transportive starting point, Alexander created a deconstructed makeup that featured heavily clumpy mascara. Layers and layers of Topshop’s False Lash Intense Mascara were applied from the bottom before squishing the lashes together with tweezers. Alexander then added a beachy pout using the burnished hue Lip Kit in Crazy Beautiful (which hits stores in March). “It’s a paint that we’re layering up in the center of the lips and then blurring out at the edges,” she explained before pulling out her secret weapon — a mattifier to give the lips a stamped-on tone that felt more natural and undone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-topshop/20tmag-topshop-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 6