8b'}, {'abstract': 'The extravagant golfer at 50 is beloved by fans awed by his refusal to stop living large. But he hopes a slow start on the senior scene is only a period of adjustment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/20/sports/golf/john-daly-pga-tour-champions.html', 'snippet': 'The extravagant golfer at 50 is beloved by fans awed by his refusal to stop living large. But he hopes a slow start on the senior scene is only a period of adjustment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAPLES, Fla. — Even at 50 years old, John Daly still draws a crowd. During the Chubb Classic pro-am on Thursday, grown men begged for selfies or a signature. One supporter of retirement age stammered like a schoolboy at his first dance, saying, “Mr. Daly, can I shake your hand?” As soon as Daly released his grip, the fan turned to his wife and said, “O.K., honey, we can go now.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/21/sports/21DALY/21DALY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Daly Gets Back in the Swing — on His Own Terms, of Course', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At 50, a Rock Star on a New Tour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daly, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PGA Championship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-20T23:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Schupak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schupak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b51d5fa-44c5-5ebf-9108-4ae00f880cd4', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b51d5fa-44c5-5ebf-9108-4ae00f880cd4'}, {'abstract': 'A retired scientist became a hero to some climate-change deniers after he criticized his former boss at NOAA over data handling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/20/business/energy-environment/climate-change-dispute-john-bates.html', 'snippet': 'A retired scientist became a hero to some climate-change deniers after he criticized his former boss at NOAA over data handling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, on an obscure climate-change blog, a retired government scientist named John Bates blasted his former boss on an esoteric point having to do with archiving temperature data.',