ay', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Constance Gustke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Constance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gustke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc400cd7-82dd-5edc-8fcd-cc915a27bbff', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc400cd7-82dd-5edc-8fcd-cc915a27bbff'}, {'abstract': 'The consumer goods company said it would seek to “accelerate delivery of value for the benefit of our shareholders” after Kraft Heinz backed away from a deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/22/business/dealbook/unilever-to-review-options-after-takeover-bid-is-withdrawn.html', 'snippet': 'The consumer goods company said it would seek to “accelerate delivery of value for the benefit of our shareholders” after Kraft Heinz backed away from a deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Unilever said on Wednesday that it was conducting a “comprehensive review” of its options after Kraft Heinz withdrew a $143 billion takeover bid for the consumer goods company on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/business/23DB-UNILEVER/23-UNILEVER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unilever to Review Options After Takeover Bid Is Withdrawn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kraft Heinz Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unilever NV', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-22T15:29:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50444f55-f4b5-538c-9e51-049602088f6f', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50444f55-f4b5-538c-9e51-049602088f6f'}, {'abstract': 'They don’t make it like they used to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/22/t-magazine/joys-of-propaganda.html', 'snippet': 'They don’t make it like they used to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to facts, some leaders, like many a florid narcissist, will build a palace and gardens around their anxieties and swear allegiance to the flag flying above them. They supplant what is true with what they wish to be true and simply deny the evidence. This is a crude modern business and has very little to do with great propaganda, which relies on something much more systematic and more artful in the organization of human wishes. The good news, however, is that propaganda is back. I don’t mean the unfragrant mob of internet miscreants — hacking is to propaganda what stalking is to romance. I mean the impulse to choose a side and press its case with wily elegance. Those of us who grew up in the Cold War have rather missed it — the persistent, well-designed, all-encompassing salesmanship of Life’s Correct Path, backed up with textbooks, posters and unspeakable stockpiles of nuclear weapons.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '56', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/05/t-magazine/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/05/t-magazine/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/05/t-magazine/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/05/t-magazine/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0/05tmag-02look_sign-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1506, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo',