': 'nyt://article/23d5e37b-dbe7-5a0a-a3fa-ecd8fae2c11b', 'word_count': 758, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23d5e37b-dbe7-5a0a-a3fa-ecd8fae2c11b'}, {'abstract': 'A meal that will please your children and satisfy an adult’s desire for flavor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/magazine/buttered-swordfish-for-finicky-kids-with-plenty-of-sauce-for-the-adults.html', 'snippet': 'A meal that will please your children and satisfy an adult’s desire for flavor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I cannot possibly count how many times I have been sought out by some mom with an urgent, hard, particular shine in her eye who wants to know, needs to know, how and what I feed my children. As I am in fact a woman, a restaurant chef and a parent of two, it’s an understandable mistake. Let me disappoint straight away: My priority has never been having kids who eat; it is about having kids who sleep. Nobody wants to get home from a restaurant job at 1:30 in the morning, stir themselves a medicinal, soporific negroni, shower off the greasy stink of a commercial kitchen and finally hit the pillow around 3 a.m., only to hear the cracking thunder of her alert and chipper darlings at 6:30 a.m. I decided I could tolerate all the Cheddar Goldfish and the years of plain buttered pasta as long as they slept till 11 a.m.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26eat-copy/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buttered Swordfish for Finicky Kids — With Plenty of Sauce for the Adults', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mother Knows Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prune (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-24T10:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c34ce750-092e-5fb3-93ad-a8a4705087d1', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c34ce750-092e-5fb3-93ad-a8a4705087d1'}, {'abstract': 'Partaking in aperitivo time, that easy stretch of sipping and snacking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/magazine/take-it-slow-for-roman-cocktail-hour.html', 'snippet': 'Partaking in aperitivo time, that easy stretch of sipping and snacking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, as I sat in an elegant hotel bar in Rome, I caught myself wondering if there can be such a thing as too much magnificence in a single place. With its antiquity (“Just go to the Colosseum, face east and shout, ‘Moira,’\u2009” my friend joked when I asked how to get to her house), its art and its food, Rome nearly overwhelmed me with its aesthetic and alimentary too-much-ness.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26drink-copy/26mag-26drink-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26drink-copy/26mag-26drink-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26drink-copy/26mag-26drink-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26drink-copy/26mag-26drink-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26drink-copy/26mag-26drink-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/magazine/26drink-c