/www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/world/asia/north-korea-kim-jong-nam-vx-nerve-agent.html', 'snippet': 'The assassination by VX nerve agent is a stark reminder that in addition to nuclear arms, Pyongyang has an arsenal of chemical and biological weapons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KUALA LUMPUR, Malaysia — For years, North Korea has rattled the world with its nuclear tests and its threats to visit a nuclear holocaust upon the United States. Now, the finding by the Malaysian police that Kim Jong-nam was assassinated with VX nerve agent is a stark reminder of the North’s lesser-known weapons of mass destruction: a stockpile of chemical and biological weapons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/world/25kim-1/25kim-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Kim Jong-nam’s Death, North Korea Lets Loose a Weapon of Mass Destruction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Killing of North Korean Offers Blunt Warning on Nation’s Deadly Arsenal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-nam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-24T15:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard C. Paddock, Choe Sang-Hun and Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Paddock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6e689bc-c80e-5bdc-b84e-21cc880a0a7e', 'word_count': 1197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6e689bc-c80e-5bdc-b84e-21cc880a0a7e'}, {'abstract': 'In some situations, they are just as cutthroat as men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/opinion/sunday/women-do-like-to-compete-against-themselves.html', 'snippet': 'In some situations, they are just as cutthroat as men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 10 years ago, when we were both Ph.D. students at Harvard, we were invited to participate in an unofficial and largely secret wrestling tournament organized by a fellow student. The idea was to showcase a handful of competitive wrestling matches between graduate students in different departments to an invitation-only audience. Space and gym mats were rented, a referee and a master of ceremonies were appointed, and monetary bets were placed on individual matches. Each wrestler had his or her own costume, entrance song and fan base. Alcohol flowed freely among the spectators.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 571, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1142, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Do Like to Compete — Against Themselves', 'kicker': 'Gray Matter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Actually, Women Do Like to Compete', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-24T15:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coren Apicella and Johanna Mollerstrom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apicella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Johanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mollerstrom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff6a6ea-c4f0-5c17-aa35-b4f85b30ce70', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff6a6ea-c4f0-5c17-aa35-b4f85b30ce70'}, {'abstract': 'A handful of designers, including Simone Rocha and Christopher Kane, are joining the ranks of the city’s “young fogies.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/old-fashioned-style-trend.html', 'snippet': 'A handful of designers, including Simone Rocha and Christopher Kane, are joining the ranks of the city’s “young fogies.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'London has a reputation for breeding young designers who generally make clothes of the unwearable variety. Their work is called “avant-garde,” meaning dresses are made of Saran Wrap or chicken feathers with leather pointy-shouldered blazers and mismatched shoes (although the much-copied Phoebe Philo of Céline showed the latter for spring/summer 2017, so maybe the lopsided look is about to go mainstream.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/23/t-magazine/fashion/23tmag-fogies/23tmag-fogies-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In London, the Rise of Old-Fashioned Fashion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None,