Shows: Prada, Fendi, Emilio Pucci, Moschino', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emilio Pucci Srl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fendi SpA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moschino SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-24T17:14:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By LAURA RYSMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RYSMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/78048df1-42a4-5536-b632-dbabb7c7399e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/78048df1-42a4-5536-b632-dbabb7c7399e'}, {'abstract': 'From backstage at Etro’s fall/winter 2017 show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/etro-eye-makeup-beauty-milan-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'From backstage at Etro’s fall/winter 2017 show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Backstage at Etro’s fall/winter 2017 show, the makeup artist Mark Carrasquillo enhanced models’ complexion with lots of moisturizer — the backbone of any natural beauty look — and a smudge of blush. And because he wanted eyes to pop but didn’t want the appearance of obvious makeup, he used the ol’ water line trick: Carrasquillo edged the inside of the upper eyelid, right along the water line, with a pencil (MAC, in Teddy — a slightly metallic, deep brown tone) before curling lashes and brushing mascara onto the upper tips. “Since it’s not on the skin, you don’t see the line of the pencil,” said Carrasquillo, noting that usually eyeliner is only applied to the lower water line. “You still get this darkness to the eyes, this added attractiveness, but without a cosmetic feel.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/24/t-magazine/fashion/24tmag-beauty/24tmag-beauty-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make Eyes Pop — Without the Appearance of Liner', 'kicker': 'Backstage Beauty Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Etro SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-24T17:18:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Rysman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rysman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c080be6a-7799-5895-8306-0519df6bda97', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c080be6a-7799-5895-8306-0519df6bda97'}, {'abstract': 'A study of DNA from 14 bodies in a burial site in New Mexico’s Chaco Canyon found a matrilineal link, raising questions about a society’s structure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/24/science/chaco-canyon-new-mexico-maternal.html', 'snippet': 'A study of DNA from 14 bodies in a burial site in New Mexico’s Chaco Canyon found a matrilineal link, raising questions about a society’s structure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a really small room in a really big house, archaeologists found the body of a 40-year-old man. They knew he was special. He was buried with a conch shell trumpet and large shells from the Pacific coast, far from this crypt in the 650-room building known as Pueblo Bonito in what is now called Chaco Canyon, in New Mexico. He was adorned with more than 11,000 beads and pendants made of turquoise and more than 3,000 made of shell. But if he was special, he was just the bottom layer.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/science/25tb-chaco01/25tb-