, New York Post-style gossip: “Page Six reporter.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Ruled the Tabloid Media. Washington Is a Different Story.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Ruled the Tabloid Media. Washington Is a Different Story.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bannon, Stephen K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spicer, Sean M (1971- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-25T17:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Thrush and Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thrush', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d36016-00b7-58aa-9fb6-204a6c7a6eb9', 'word_count': 1501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d36016-00b7-58aa-9fb6-204a6c7a6eb9'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s war on the media emboldens autocrats who kill and imprison journalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/25/opinion/trump-is-damaging-press-freedom-in-the-us-and-abroad.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s war on the media emboldens autocrats who kill and imprison journalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Speaking at the Conservative Political Action Conference Friday, President Trump took his anti-media rhetoric to a new level, doubling down on his description of journalists as “the enemy of the people” and calling for an end to the use of anonymous sources. This on a day when his press secretary Sean Spicer barred reporters from The New York Times, BBC, BuzzFeed News, CNN, Politico, The Los Angeles Times and The Huffington Post from his daily White House press briefing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 487}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/25/opinion/25joelsimon/25joelsimon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1661, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Is Damaging Press Freedom in the U.S. and Abroad', 'k