e': 'Stone, Emma', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Denzel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Arrival (Movie)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fences (Movie)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hacksaw Ridge (Movie)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hell or High Water (Movie)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hidden Figures (Movie)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La La Land (Movie)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lion (Movie)', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Moonlight (Movie)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Manchester by the Sea (Movie)', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-25T21:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Suderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c0954b1-a769-554b-82f8-74618d881aa1', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c0954b1-a769-554b-82f8-74618d881aa1'}, {'abstract': '“La La Land” brings movie musicals into the 21st century with a reality check.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/25/opinion/sunday/escaping-to-la-la-land-then-and-now.html', 'snippet': '“La La Land” brings movie musicals into the 21st century with a reality check.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1930s, Hollywood studios produced more than 400 movie musicals. The total for 1936 alone was over 50, including two films (“Follow the Fleet” and “Swing Time”) starring Fred Astaire and Ginger Rogers. Eighty years later, in 2016, there were all of four, which isn’t many by comparison but is three more than most of us would have guessed. “La La Land” has so dominated the theaters and the headlines that you could be forgiven for thinking that it’s the first and only movie musical to come along in years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 791}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/26brubach1web/26brubach1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1553, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Escaping to La La Land, Then and Now', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astaire, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chazelle, Damien', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Ginger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Emma', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La La Land (Movie)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-25T21:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Brubach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brubach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/44fe00ff-b078-52f1-85c6-a1b97df43e0f', 'word_count': 1685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44fe00ff-b078-52f1-85c6-a1b97df43e0f'}, {'abstract': 'There may be good reasons to worry, but they’re not the ones everyone is giving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/25/opinion/what-does-steve-bannon-want.html', 'snippet': 'There may be good reasons to worry, but they’re not the ones everyone is giving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump presents a problem to those who look at politics in terms of systematic ideologies. He is either disinclined or unable to lay out his agenda in that way. So perhaps it was inevitable that Mr. Trump’s chief strategist, Stephen K. Bannon, who does have a gift for thinking systematically, would be so often invoked by Mr. Trump’s opponents. They need him not just as a hate object but as a heuristic, too. There may never be a “Trumpism,” and unless one emerges, the closest we may come to understanding this administration is as an expression of “Bannonism.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 871}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/26/opinion/sunday/26caldwell/26caldwell-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1412, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does Steve Bannon Want?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Does Stev