ming to U.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Shootings of Two Engineers,  Indians Are Wary of Moving to the U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Olathe (Kan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuchibhotla, Srinivas (d 2017)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Purinton, Adam W', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madasani, Alok', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-26T21:37:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry and Nida Najar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Najar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b414f26-b6f7-5269-a8d0-fad97164eef4', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b414f26-b6f7-5269-a8d0-fad97164eef4'}, {'abstract': 'It is unclear if the president is aware of the historic resonance of the label, but his use of it has left some historians scratching their heads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/26/world/europe/trump-enemy-of-the-people-stalin.html', 'snippet': 'It is unclear if the president is aware of the historic resonance of the label, but his use of it has left some historians scratching their heads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The phrase was too toxic even for Nikita Khrushchev, a war-hardened veteran communist not known for squeamishness. As leader of the Soviet Union, he demanded an end to the use of the term “enemy of the people” because “it eliminated the possibility of any kind of ideological fight.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/world/27enemy1/27enemy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1221, 'width':