m with a workshop for convicts and a show at the Sing Sing Correctional Facility in Ossining, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/26/arts/music/rhiannon-giddens-celebrates-freedom-highway-in-the-big-house.html', 'snippet': 'The folk singer accompanied the release of a new album with a workshop for convicts and a show at the Sing Sing Correctional Facility in Ossining, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSSINING, N.Y. — The music industry usually rolls out new albums with in-store performances at record shops, high-profile media appearances or buzzworthy kickoff concerts. But when Nonesuch Records released “Freedom Highway,” the new album by the folk singer Rhiannon Giddens, on Feb. 24, the occasion was marked by Ms. Giddens and her backing band’s spending a day in a far more sobering environment: the Sing Sing Correctional Facility.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rhiannon Giddens Celebrates ‘Freedom Highway’ in the Big House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inspiring the Souls of the Incarcerated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giddens, Rhiannon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sing Sing Correctional Facility', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Freedom Highway (Album)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-27T01:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92bccbcb-880c-551c-99f0-4ba166ab0c84', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92bccbcb-880c-551c-99f0-4ba166ab0c84'}, {'abstract': 'Leading by four strokes headed into Sunday’s final round, Fowler overcame trouble on the front nine and held off Gary Woodland and Morgan Hoffmann.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/26/sports/golf/rickie-fowler-honda-classic-pga.html', 'snippet': 'Leading by four strokes headed into Sunday’s final round, Fowler overcame trouble on the front nine and held off Gary Woodland and Morgan Hoffmann.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALM BEACH GARDENS, Fla. — On his front nine Sunday at the Honda Classic, Rickie Fowler called to mind a sailor trying to hold a steady course in a stiff headwind. The final round is not always a Sunday cruise for the leader — in the first 14 tournaments of this wraparound season, the player with at least a share of the third-round lead held on to win just six times. But Fowler’s course was complicated by uncharted waters: He had never won on the PGA Tour after entering the final round ahead.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/27/sports/27GOLF/27GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rickie Fowler Weathers a Storm to Win the Honda Classic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struggling Fowler Finds a Rudder, and a Victory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fowler, Rickie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffmann, Morgan (1989- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodland, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-27T01:14:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a3ebe59-42ae-561e-a058-c34836ba30c8', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a3ebe59-42ae-561e-a058-c34836ba30c8'}, {'abstract': 'Busch’s victory, in his 17th try, came in a race marred by crashes, including a 17-car wreck. Ryan Blaney took second after Chase Elliott, who led for 38 laps, ran out of gas with two to go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/26/sports/kurt-busch-daytona-500.html', 'snippet': 'Busch’s victo