e country heal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When combatants lay down their weapons, it’s merely the beginning of peace. The harder task, especially in a conflict that has dragged on for decades, it to find social peace. The Spanish photographer Alvaro Ybarra found that to be the case in Colombia, where lawmakers last year approved a peace accord with the FARC rebels. Not only does each side have its own grievances, he said, but there often are vastly different perceptions of the conflict, with people living in bustling cities unaware of the hardships facing their countrymen in remote areas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking at All Sides in Colombia’s Conflict', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia Marquez, Gabriel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-02-27T10:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2218e53-1aed-55ab-aea5-cb7d67a04a5c', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2218e53-1aed-55ab-aea5-cb7d67a04a5c'}, {'abstract': 'Look closely at this image, stripped of its caption, and join the moderated conversation about what you and other students see.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/27/learning/whats-going-on-in-this-picture-feb-27-2017.html', 'snippet': 'Look closely at this image, stripped of its caption, and join the moderated conversation about what you and other students see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated: Marc